window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b124-155ed50bdbe182a6.json"]={sha256:"155ed50bdbe182a63dcdb338649d2d93170a267d628d73fd815108cde6936450",value:{"id":"b124","title":"首都圈外郭放水路","titleEn":"Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"首都圈外郭放水路由入流設施、地下水路、調壓水槽與泵站共同減少洪水影響，官方圖列水路6.3公里。2002年先行運用的是部分3.3公里區間，工程期至2006年。本課以水量、能量及水位基準串接全系統，避免把地下河道誤當道路隧道或將局部算例當完整洪水演算。","summaryEn":"The Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel combines intakes, a 6.3 km underground waterway, a pressure-control tank and pumps. Interim use in 2002 covered a 3.3 km portion; construction continued to 2006. This course connects water balance, energy and level datum without treating the facility as a road or a local calculation as full flood routing.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["水體平流時間","Water advection time"],["淨入流調蓄量","Net-inflow storage"],["跌水位能通量","Drop potential-energy flux"],["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["水位零點偏差","Level zero-point bias"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["水體平流時間","淨入流調蓄量","跌水位能通量","測壓水頭","水位零點偏差"],"labelsEn":["Water advection time","Net-inflow storage","Drop potential-energy flux","Piezometric head","Level zero-point bias"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「洪水歷線與調蓄餘量」，再獨立計算「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」。原創教學假設：入流=173 m³/s；出流=100 m³/s；時間段=20 min。ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³。僅把入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為108360 m³。邊界：矩形歷線單一時段，真實洪水需逐時積分與水位約束；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=127 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1370.46 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate flood hydrographs and storage reserve, then independently calculate piezometric head and lining pressure. Original teaching assumptions: inflow=173 m³/s; outflow=100 m³/s; interval=20 min. ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³. Increasing only inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 108360 m³. Boundary: One rectangular-hydrograph interval; real floods need time integration and level constraints. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=127 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1370.46 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b124-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「地下水路與傳遞時間」與「洪水歷線與調蓄餘量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Underground water routes and travel time\" and \"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b124-v14-01","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「水體平流時間」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water advection time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"首都圈放水路收集多河川入流，教材以水體平流時間辨認路徑，明確區別洪峰波速與控制延遲。地下排水或引水設施的路線先由集水區、入流點、出口水位及坡度定義，不能以交通旅行時間衡量。定速水體的行程可用距離除速度估算，但洪峰波速、蓄水與回水會改變訊號傳遞；各支路必須在共同水位與時間基準下連接。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水體平流時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The channel receives several rivers; use material advection to identify a route while distinguishing flood-wave celerity and control delay. An underground water route is defined by catchments, inflows, outfall level and gradient, not vehicle journey time. Distance divided by velocity estimates constant-speed material travel, while flood-wave celerity, storage and backwater alter signal propagation. Branches must be connected using common level and time references before interpreting arrival or control response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water advection time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水路長度=2350 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2350 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=26.1111 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水體平流時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water advection time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-01-k1","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time","text":"首都圈放水路收集多河川入流，教材以水體平流時間辨認路徑，明確區別洪峰波速與控制延遲。地下排水或引水設施的路線先由集水區、入流點、出口水位及坡度定義，不能以交通旅行時間衡量。","textEn":"The channel receives several rivers; use material advection to identify a route while distinguishing flood-wave celerity and control delay. An underground water route is defined by catchments, inflows, outfall level and gradient, not vehicle journey time.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地下水路與傳遞時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Underground water routes and travel time\" is correct?","options":["水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。","首都圈放水路收集多河川入流，教材以水體平流時間辨認路徑，明確區別洪峰波速與控制延遲。","泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。"],"optionsEn":["Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.","The channel receives several rivers; use material advection to identify a route while distinguishing flood-wave celerity and control delay.","Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"首都圈放水路收集多河川入流，教材以水體平流時間辨認路徑，明確區別洪峰波速與控制延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The channel receives several rivers; use material advection to identify a route while distinguishing flood-wave celerity and control delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b124-v14-02","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水體平流時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water advection time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水路長度=2350 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。t=L/v/60=26.1111 min。僅把水路長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為28.7222 min。邊界：定速水體平流，不是洪峰波速或完整洪水演算；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2350 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=26.1111 min. Increasing only reach length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 28.7222 min. Boundary: Constant-speed water advection, not flood-wave celerity or complete routing. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align branch and outlet flow-level histories.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水路長度=2350 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。t=L/v/60=26.1111 min。僅把水路長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為28.7222 min。邊界：定速水體平流，不是洪峰波速或完整洪水演算；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2350 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=26.1111 min. Increasing only reach length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 28.7222 min. Boundary: Constant-speed water advection, not flood-wave celerity or complete routing. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地下水路與傳遞時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Underground water routes and travel time\", which statement holds?","options":["跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：水路長度=2350 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2350 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=26.1111 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水路長度=2350 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2350 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=26.1111 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b124-v14-03","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水體平流時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water advection time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。對齊入口與出口水位流量時間序列，利用允許的示蹤或模型比較平流時間與洪峰時差，保留回水條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align branch and outlet flow-level histories. Align inlet and outlet level-flow histories; use permitted tracer data or modelling to distinguish material travel from peak lag while preserving backwater conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「水體平流時間」的交付需回答：對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。路線圖同時標示水位基準、支路與控制邊界，所有時間比較註明是物質、波峰或設備延遲，避免混用。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the water advection time handover must address the following evidence: Align branch and outlet flow-level histories. Route diagrams show level datum, branches and control boundaries; label each time as material travel, wave propagation or equipment delay.","failure":"注意干擾：用交通速度或單一平流時間預測洪峰都會失去水理意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Vehicle speed or one advection time cannot predict flood-peak routing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。對齊入口與出口水位流量時間序列，利用允許的示蹤或模型比較平流時間與洪峰時差，保留回水條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align branch and outlet flow-level histories. Align inlet and outlet level-flow histories; use permitted tracer data or modelling to distinguish material travel from peak lag while preserving backwater conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「水體平流時間」的交付需回答：對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。路線圖同時標示水位基準、支路與控制邊界，所有時間比較註明是物質、波峰或設備延遲，避免混用。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the water advection time handover must address the following evidence: Align branch and outlet flow-level histories. Route diagrams show level datum, branches and control boundaries; label each time as material travel, wave propagation or equipment delay.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地下水路與傳遞時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Underground water routes and travel time\"?","options":["對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Align branch and outlet flow-level histories.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對齊各支路和出口的流量水位時序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align branch and outlet flow-level histories. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b124-v14-04","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水體平流時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water advection time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用交通速度或單一平流時間預測洪峰都會失去水理意義。把平流時間當洪峰預警時間會忽略波速和支路入流，控制指令可能在假定水體到達之前已失去適用性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Vehicle speed or one advection time cannot predict flood-peak routing. Using advection time as flood-warning time ignores celerity and side inflows, allowing control assumptions to fail before the assumed arrival. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：定速水體的行程可用距離除速度估算，但洪峰波速、蓄水與回水會改變訊號傳遞；各支路必須在共同水位與時間基準下連接。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Branches must be connected using common level and time references before interpreting arrival or control response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用交通速度或單一平流時間預測洪峰都會失去水理意義。把平流時間當洪峰預警時間會忽略波速和支路入流，控制指令可能在假定水體到達之前已失去適用性。","textEn":"Vehicle speed or one advection time cannot predict flood-peak routing. Using advection time as flood-warning time ignores celerity and side inflows, allowing control assumptions to fail before the assumed arrival.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地下水路與傳遞時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Underground water routes and travel time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用交通速度或單一平流時間預測洪峰都會失去水理意義。","泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Vehicle speed or one advection time cannot predict flood-peak routing.","Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用交通速度或單一平流時間預測洪峰都會失去水理意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Vehicle speed or one advection time cannot predict flood-peak routing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b124-v14-05","title":"洪水歷線與調蓄餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「淨入流調蓄量」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Net-inflow storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"調蓄量由入出流歷線積分決定，教材研究下游高水位限制排放時的庫容消耗。調蓄設施以流入減流出的時間積分決定蓄水變化，最大入流量並不單獨決定所需庫容。下游高水位可能限制排水，水位與可用庫容也不是固定比例；需同時檢查初始蓄水、泵站可用性與洪水歷線的時序。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「淨入流調蓄量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Storage follows integrated inflow minus outflow; examine reserve depletion when downstream high water limits discharge. Storage change is the time integral of inflow minus outflow, so peak inflow alone cannot determine required capacity. High downstream levels can restrict discharge, and level is not always proportional to volume. Initial occupancy, pump availability and hydrograph timing must be assessed together rather than assuming the facility starts empty with unrestricted outflow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Net-inflow storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：入流=173 m³/s；出流=100 m³/s；時間段=20 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: inflow=173 m³/s; outflow=100 m³/s; interval=20 min. ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「淨入流調蓄量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Net-inflow storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-05-k1","title":"洪水歷線與調蓄餘量","titleEn":"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve","text":"調蓄量由入出流歷線積分決定，教材研究下游高水位限制排放時的庫容消耗。調蓄設施以流入減流出的時間積分決定蓄水變化，最大入流量並不單獨決定所需庫容。","textEn":"Storage follows integrated inflow minus outflow; examine reserve depletion when downstream high water limits discharge. Storage change is the time integral of inflow minus outflow, so peak inflow alone cannot determine required capacity.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「洪水歷線與調蓄餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve\" is correct?","options":["泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","調蓄量由入出流歷線積分決定，教材研究下游高水位限制排放時的庫容消耗。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Storage follows integrated inflow minus outflow; examine reserve depletion when downstream high water limits discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"調蓄量由入出流歷線積分決定，教材研究下游高水位限制排放時的庫容消耗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Storage follows integrated inflow minus outflow; examine reserve depletion when downstream high water limits discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b124-v14-06","title":"洪水歷線與調蓄餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「淨入流調蓄量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Net-inflow storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：入流=173 m³/s；出流=100 m³/s；時間段=20 min。ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³。僅把入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為108360 m³。邊界：矩形歷線單一時段，真實洪水需逐時積分與水位約束；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: inflow=173 m³/s; outflow=100 m³/s; interval=20 min. ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³. Increasing only inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 108360 m³. Boundary: One rectangular-hydrograph interval; real floods need time integration and level constraints. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：入流=173 m³/s；出流=100 m³/s；時間段=20 min。ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³。僅把入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為108360 m³。邊界：矩形歷線單一時段，真實洪水需逐時積分與水位約束；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: inflow=173 m³/s; outflow=100 m³/s; interval=20 min. ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³. Increasing only inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 108360 m³. Boundary: One rectangular-hydrograph interval; real floods need time integration and level constraints. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「洪水歷線與調蓄餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：入流=173 m³/s；出流=100 m³/s；時間段=20 min。","頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: inflow=173 m³/s; outflow=100 m³/s; interval=20 min. ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³.","Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：入流=173 m³/s；出流=100 m³/s；時間段=20 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: inflow=173 m³/s; outflow=100 m³/s; interval=20 min. ΔV=(Qin−Qout)Δt×60=87600 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b124-v14-07","title":"洪水歷線與調蓄餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「淨入流調蓄量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Net-inflow storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。將入出流歷線與水位庫容曲線閉合，測試不同初始水位和下游回水，檢查流量資料的時間間隔。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained. Close inflow-outflow hydrographs against the level-volume curve, test initial levels and downstream backwater and check sampling intervals. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「淨入流調蓄量」的交付需回答：閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。交付可重算的逐時水量帳，標記起始水位、泵狀態與邊界洪水；控制決策依核准模型和即時量測而非單段算式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the net-inflow storage handover must address the following evidence: Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained. Deliver a reproducible time-step balance with initial level, pump state and boundary flood; control decisions use approved models and observations, not one interval.","failure":"注意干擾：假設設施全空且泵始終滿流會低估最高水位。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming empty storage and full pumping throughout understates maximum level. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。將入出流歷線與水位庫容曲線閉合，測試不同初始水位和下游回水，檢查流量資料的時間間隔。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained. Close inflow-outflow hydrographs against the level-volume curve, test initial levels and downstream backwater and check sampling intervals. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「淨入流調蓄量」的交付需回答：閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。交付可重算的逐時水量帳，標記起始水位、泵狀態與邊界洪水；控制決策依核准模型和即時量測而非單段算式。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the net-inflow storage handover must address the following evidence: Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained. Deliver a reproducible time-step balance with initial level, pump state and boundary flood; control decisions use approved models and observations, not one interval.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「洪水歷線與調蓄餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閉合水位庫容和逐時流量帳，保留初始蓄水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Close level-volume and time-step flow balances with initial storage retained. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b124-v14-08","title":"洪水歷線與調蓄餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「淨入流調蓄量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Net-inflow storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"假設設施全空且泵始終滿流會低估最高水位。以日平均流量代替短時洪峰會低估最高水位，泵可用卻無法克服下游水頭也會造成錯誤出流假設。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming empty storage and full pumping throughout understates maximum level. Daily mean flow misses short peaks and underestimates maximum level; an available pump may still fail to discharge against the downstream head. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下游高水位可能限制排水，水位與可用庫容也不是固定比例；需同時檢查初始蓄水、泵站可用性與洪水歷線的時序。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Initial occupancy, pump availability and hydrograph timing must be assessed together rather than assuming the facility starts empty with unrestricted outflow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"假設設施全空且泵始終滿流會低估最高水位。以日平均流量代替短時洪峰會低估最高水位，泵可用卻無法克服下游水頭也會造成錯誤出流假設。","textEn":"Assuming empty storage and full pumping throughout understates maximum level. Daily mean flow misses short peaks and underestimates maximum level; an available pump may still fail to discharge against the downstream head.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「洪水歷線與調蓄餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flood hydrographs and storage reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","假設設施全空且泵始終滿流會低估最高水位。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Assuming empty storage and full pumping throughout understates maximum level."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設設施全空且泵始終滿流會低估最高水位。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming empty storage and full pumping throughout understates maximum level. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b124-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」與「豎井跌水與能量消散」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\" and \"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b124-v14-09","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「滿管沿程損失」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Full-pipe friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地下水路的摩阻算例限穩態滿管，教材另外辨認自由水面、回水和局部收縮可能改變流況。輸水隧道由上下游能量差驅動，沿程粗糙度、接頭及局部收縮消耗水頭；流速增加使摩阻快速上升。穩態滿管式不能描述水錘、自由水面轉換或氣囊，閘門動作和停機歷程必須另外建立瞬變模型與通氣條件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滿管沿程損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The friction example is steady and full-pipe; identify free surfaces, backwater and contractions that can change the flow regime. A conveyance tunnel is driven by upstream and downstream energy levels; roughness, joints and contractions consume head, with friction rising rapidly with velocity. A steady full-pipe equation does not describe water hammer, free-surface transitions or trapped air. Gate movements and shutdown histories require separate transient modelling and explicit ventilation conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Full-pipe friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=2150 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=2150 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滿管沿程損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Full-pipe friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-09-k1","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries","text":"地下水路的摩阻算例限穩態滿管，教材另外辨認自由水面、回水和局部收縮可能改變流況。輸水隧道由上下游能量差驅動，沿程粗糙度、接頭及局部收縮消耗水頭；流速增加使摩阻快速上升。","textEn":"The friction example is steady and full-pipe; identify free surfaces, backwater and contractions that can change the flow regime. A conveyance tunnel is driven by upstream and downstream energy levels; roughness, joints and contractions consume head, with friction rising rapidly with velocity.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\" is correct?","options":["地下水路的摩阻算例限穩態滿管，教材另外辨認自由水面、回水和局部收縮可能改變流況。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。"],"optionsEn":["The friction example is steady and full-pipe; identify free surfaces, backwater and contractions that can change the flow regime.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地下水路的摩阻算例限穩態滿管，教材另外辨認自由水面、回水和局部收縮可能改變流況。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The friction example is steady and full-pipe; identify free surfaces, backwater and contractions that can change the flow regime. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b124-v14-10","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滿管沿程損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Full-pipe friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=2150 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m。僅把流速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2.65189 m。邊界：滿管穩態摩阻，不含水錘與局部損失；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=2150 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m. Increasing only velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2.65189 m. Boundary: Steady full-pipe friction, excluding water hammer and local loss. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=2150 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m。僅把流速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2.65189 m。邊界：滿管穩態摩阻，不含水錘與局部損失；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=2150 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m. Increasing only velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2.65189 m. Boundary: Steady full-pipe friction, excluding water hammer and local loss. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=2150 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。","多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=2150 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m.","Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=2150 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=2150 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=2.19164 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b124-v14-11","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滿管沿程損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Full-pipe friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。以同步上下游水位和流量核對能量坡度，分辨入口損失與沿程損失，保留閘門及氣壓狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states. Use synchronised levels and flow to check energy gradient, separate entrance from distributed losses and preserve gate and air-pressure states. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「滿管沿程損失」的交付需回答：以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。水理交付需包含水位基準、流量、閘門歷程及模型適用狀態；瞬變與通氣由水理設計者另行檢核。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the full-pipe friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states. Hydraulic handover includes level datum, flow, gate histories and model regimes; specialists independently assess transients and air movement.","failure":"注意干擾：在非滿管時套滿管直徑會得到無物理邊界的損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using full-pipe geometry in free-surface flow gives an inapplicable loss estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。以同步上下游水位和流量核對能量坡度，分辨入口損失與沿程損失，保留閘門及氣壓狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states. Use synchronised levels and flow to check energy gradient, separate entrance from distributed losses and preserve gate and air-pressure states. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「滿管沿程損失」的交付需回答：以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。水理交付需包含水位基準、流量、閘門歷程及模型適用狀態；瞬變與通氣由水理設計者另行檢核。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the full-pipe friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states. Hydraulic handover includes level datum, flow, gate histories and model regimes; specialists independently assess transients and air movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以同步水位和流量辨認滿管及非滿管狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use simultaneous levels and flow to distinguish pressurised and free-surface states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b124-v14-12","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滿管沿程損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Full-pipe friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在非滿管時套滿管直徑會得到無物理邊界的損失。把閘門急動後的壓力峰當穩態摩阻，會錯估粗糙度並漏掉瞬變作用；未排出的氣囊也會改變有效斷面。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using full-pipe geometry in free-surface flow gives an inapplicable loss estimate. Treating post-gate pressure peaks as steady friction biases roughness and misses transients; trapped air also changes effective area. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：穩態滿管式不能描述水錘、自由水面轉換或氣囊，閘門動作和停機歷程必須另外建立瞬變模型與通氣條件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Gate movements and shutdown histories require separate transient modelling and explicit ventilation conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在非滿管時套滿管直徑會得到無物理邊界的損失。把閘門急動後的壓力峰當穩態摩阻，會錯估粗糙度並漏掉瞬變作用；未排出的氣囊也會改變有效斷面。","textEn":"Using full-pipe geometry in free-surface flow gives an inapplicable loss estimate. Treating post-gate pressure peaks as steady friction biases roughness and misses transients; trapped air also changes effective area.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["在非滿管時套滿管直徑會得到無物理邊界的損失。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Using full-pipe geometry in free-surface flow gives an inapplicable loss estimate.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在非滿管時套滿管直徑會得到無物理邊界的損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using full-pipe geometry in free-surface flow gives an inapplicable loss estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b124-v14-13","title":"豎井跌水與能量消散：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「跌水位能通量」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drop potential-energy flux” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"入流豎井把高程能轉成紊流和壓力，教材算位能通量而不是提升機功率或井壁均壓。水流進入豎井時把高程能轉成速度、紊流與壓力波動，空氣捲入和排氣路徑會改變流況。位能通量只能估計需處理的能量量級，不能由此直接求井壁衝擊壓；進流偏心、淹沒與下游回水需實體或數值水理驗證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跌水位能通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inlet shafts convert elevation energy into turbulence and pressure; calculate potential-energy flux rather than hoist power or uniform wall pressure. Flow entering a shaft converts elevation energy into velocity, turbulence and fluctuating pressure, while entrainment and ventilation change the regime. Potential-energy flux estimates the scale to be dissipated but cannot directly give wall impact pressure. Eccentric entry, submergence and downstream backwater require physical or numerical hydraulic validation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drop potential-energy flux” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；流量=20 m³/s；跌水高度=30 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; flow=20 m³/s; drop=30 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跌水位能通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drop potential-energy flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-13-k1","title":"豎井跌水與能量消散","titleEn":"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation","text":"入流豎井把高程能轉成紊流和壓力，教材算位能通量而不是提升機功率或井壁均壓。水流進入豎井時把高程能轉成速度、紊流與壓力波動，空氣捲入和排氣路徑會改變流況。","textEn":"Inlet shafts convert elevation energy into turbulence and pressure; calculate potential-energy flux rather than hoist power or uniform wall pressure. Flow entering a shaft converts elevation energy into velocity, turbulence and fluctuating pressure, while entrainment and ventilation change the regime.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「豎井跌水與能量消散」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation\" is correct?","options":["跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。","入流豎井把高程能轉成紊流和壓力，教材算位能通量而不是提升機功率或井壁均壓。","頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。"],"optionsEn":["Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure.","Inlet shafts convert elevation energy into turbulence and pressure; calculate potential-energy flux rather than hoist power or uniform wall pressure.","Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入流豎井把高程能轉成紊流和壓力，教材算位能通量而不是提升機功率或井壁均壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inlet shafts convert elevation energy into turbulence and pressure; calculate potential-energy flux rather than hoist power or uniform wall pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b124-v14-14","title":"豎井跌水與能量消散：定量估算","titleEn":"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跌水位能通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drop potential-energy flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；流量=20 m³/s；跌水高度=30 m。P=ρgQH/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=5886 kW。僅把流量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6474.6 kW。邊界：位能通量，不是井壁壓力或發電輸出；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; flow=20 m³/s; drop=30 m. P=ρgQH/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=5886 kW. Increasing only flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6474.6 kW. Boundary: Potential-energy flux, not shaft-wall pressure or electrical output. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；流量=20 m³/s；跌水高度=30 m。P=ρgQH/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=5886 kW。僅把流量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6474.6 kW。邊界：位能通量，不是井壁壓力或發電輸出；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; flow=20 m³/s; drop=30 m. P=ρgQH/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=5886 kW. Increasing only flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6474.6 kW. Boundary: Potential-energy flux, not shaft-wall pressure or electrical output. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「豎井跌水與能量消散」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；流量=20 m³/s；跌水高度=30 m。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; flow=20 m³/s; drop=30 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；流量=20 m³/s；跌水高度=30 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; flow=20 m³/s; drop=30 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b124-v14-15","title":"豎井跌水與能量消散：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跌水位能通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drop potential-energy flux” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。同步量測進出流、水位、井內氣壓和局部壓力脈動，比較淹沒前後工況並檢查取樣頻率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations. Synchronise flow, levels, internal air pressure and local pressure fluctuations, comparing submerged and free discharge with adequate sampling frequency. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「跌水位能通量」的交付需回答：同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。分開交付能量帳、局部壓力和通氣模型，任何流況切換都核對上下游與氣相邊界，不以提升機功率代替水理分析。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the drop potential-energy flux handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations. Deliver energy balance, local-pressure and ventilation models separately; check liquid and air boundaries at regime changes rather than substituting hoist-power calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：平均功率不能直接推出井壁最大衝擊壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mean power cannot directly yield peak wall impact pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。同步量測進出流、水位、井內氣壓和局部壓力脈動，比較淹沒前後工況並檢查取樣頻率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations. Synchronise flow, levels, internal air pressure and local pressure fluctuations, comparing submerged and free discharge with adequate sampling frequency. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「跌水位能通量」的交付需回答：同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。分開交付能量帳、局部壓力和通氣模型，任何流況切換都核對上下游與氣相邊界，不以提升機功率代替水理分析。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the drop potential-energy flux handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations. Deliver energy balance, local-pressure and ventilation models separately; check liquid and air boundaries at regime changes rather than substituting hoist-power calculations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「豎井跌水與能量消散」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation\"?","options":["同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量測跌水流量、氣壓和局部壓力脈動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise drop flow, air pressure and local pressure fluctuations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b124-v14-16","title":"豎井跌水與能量消散：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跌水位能通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drop potential-energy flux” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均功率不能直接推出井壁最大衝擊壓。忽略氣路阻塞會低估水位及壓力波動，僅用平均能量可能掩蓋局部衝擊和間歇流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mean power cannot directly yield peak wall impact pressure. Ignoring a blocked air path underestimates level and pressure fluctuations; average energy can conceal local impact and intermittent flow. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：位能通量只能估計需處理的能量量級，不能由此直接求井壁衝擊壓；進流偏心、淹沒與下游回水需實體或數值水理驗證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Eccentric entry, submergence and downstream backwater require physical or numerical hydraulic validation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均功率不能直接推出井壁最大衝擊壓。忽略氣路阻塞會低估水位及壓力波動，僅用平均能量可能掩蓋局部衝擊和間歇流。","textEn":"Mean power cannot directly yield peak wall impact pressure. Ignoring a blocked air path underestimates level and pressure fluctuations; average energy can conceal local impact and intermittent flow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「豎井跌水與能量消散」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drop-shaft flow and energy dissipation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","平均功率不能直接推出井壁最大衝擊壓。","頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mean power cannot directly yield peak wall impact pressure.","Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均功率不能直接推出井壁最大衝擊壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mean power cannot directly yield peak wall impact pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b124-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「地下大廳頂板與支承」與「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Underground hall roofs and supports\" and \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b124-v14-17","title":"地下大廳頂板與支承：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Underground hall roofs and supports: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「頂板荷載傳遞」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roof load transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"調壓大廳頂板經柱網傳力，教材條帶彎矩不取代整體框架、柱頭沖切和底板抗浮。大型地下調壓或蓄水大廳的頂板把覆土和自身重量傳到柱牆，再傳給基礎；水壓改變時底板與頂板的作用也不同。單向條帶只是局部彎矩示例，柱網、沖切、框架拘束、基礎變形及施工回填順序都需要整體模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頂板荷載傳遞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The pressure-control hall roof transfers load through columns; strip bending does not replace global, punching or flotation checks. A large underground pressure-control or storage hall transfers overburden and self-weight through its roof into columns, walls and foundations. Changing water pressure affects roof and base differently. A one-way strip illustrates local bending only; column layout, punching, frame restraint, foundation movement and backfilling sequence require a global structural model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roof load transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=43 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=43 kN/m; span=3.6 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頂板荷載傳遞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roof load transfer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-17-k1","title":"地下大廳頂板與支承","titleEn":"Underground hall roofs and supports","text":"調壓大廳頂板經柱網傳力，教材條帶彎矩不取代整體框架、柱頭沖切和底板抗浮。大型地下調壓或蓄水大廳的頂板把覆土和自身重量傳到柱牆，再傳給基礎；水壓改變時底板與頂板的作用也不同。","textEn":"The pressure-control hall roof transfers load through columns; strip bending does not replace global, punching or flotation checks. A large underground pressure-control or storage hall transfers overburden and self-weight through its roof into columns, walls and foundations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地下大廳頂板與支承」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Underground hall roofs and supports\" is correct?","options":["頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","調壓大廳頂板經柱網傳力，教材條帶彎矩不取代整體框架、柱頭沖切和底板抗浮。"],"optionsEn":["Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","The pressure-control hall roof transfers load through columns; strip bending does not replace global, punching or flotation checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"調壓大廳頂板經柱網傳力，教材條帶彎矩不取代整體框架、柱頭沖切和底板抗浮。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The pressure-control hall roof transfers load through columns; strip bending does not replace global, punching or flotation checks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b124-v14-18","title":"地下大廳頂板與支承：定量估算","titleEn":"Underground hall roofs and supports: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂板荷載傳遞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roof load transfer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=43 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。M=qL²/8=69.66 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.2886 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=43 kN/m; span=3.6 m. M=qL²/8=69.66 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.2886 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=43 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。M=qL²/8=69.66 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.2886 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=43 kN/m; span=3.6 m. M=qL²/8=69.66 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.2886 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地下大廳頂板與支承」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Underground hall roofs and supports\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：單位長載重=43 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。","多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: line load=43 kN/m; span=3.6 m.","Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=43 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=43 kN/m; span=3.6 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b124-v14-19","title":"地下大廳頂板與支承：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Underground hall roofs and supports: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂板荷載傳遞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roof load transfer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。核對柱網、板厚及回填紀錄，將柱軸力、板撓度與裂縫位置聯合判讀，不把單一應變點視為整體反應。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force. Check the column grid, slab thickness and backfill records; interpret column force, deflection and cracking together rather than treating one strain reading as global behaviour. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「頂板荷載傳遞」的交付需回答：核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。將條帶計算標為局部示範，另列整體框架、沖切和抗浮的證據需求，施工與水位階段各自核對荷載。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the roof load transfer handover must address the following evidence: Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force. Label the strip calculation as local and list global frame, punching and flotation evidence separately, reconciling loads for each construction and water-level stage.","failure":"注意干擾：頂板均載模型不能用來宣稱整個大廳抗浮穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A uniformly loaded roof model cannot establish flotation stability of the hall. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。核對柱網、板厚及回填紀錄，將柱軸力、板撓度與裂縫位置聯合判讀，不把單一應變點視為整體反應。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force. Check the column grid, slab thickness and backfill records; interpret column force, deflection and cracking together rather than treating one strain reading as global behaviour. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「頂板荷載傳遞」的交付需回答：核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。將條帶計算標為局部示範，另列整體框架、沖切和抗浮的證據需求，施工與水位階段各自核對荷載。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the roof load transfer handover must address the following evidence: Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force. Label the strip calculation as local and list global frame, punching and flotation evidence separately, reconciling loads for each construction and water-level stage.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地下大廳頂板與支承」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Underground hall roofs and supports\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。","泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force.","Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對柱網、回填、板撓度與柱軸力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check column layout, backfill, slab deflection and column force. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b124-v14-20","title":"地下大廳頂板與支承：失效診斷","titleEn":"Underground hall roofs and supports: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂板荷載傳遞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roof load transfer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"頂板均載模型不能用來宣稱整個大廳抗浮穩定。漏掉局部柱頭作用會在平均彎矩不大時仍低估沖切風險，差異沉陷則可能把荷載重新分配到少數支承。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A uniformly loaded roof model cannot establish flotation stability of the hall. Missing column-head effects underestimates punching despite modest mean bending, while differential settlement redistributes load to fewer supports. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單向條帶只是局部彎矩示例，柱網、沖切、框架拘束、基礎變形及施工回填順序都需要整體模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A one-way strip illustrates local bending only; column layout, punching, frame restraint, foundation movement and backfilling sequence require a global structural model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"頂板均載模型不能用來宣稱整個大廳抗浮穩定。漏掉局部柱頭作用會在平均彎矩不大時仍低估沖切風險，差異沉陷則可能把荷載重新分配到少數支承。","textEn":"A uniformly loaded roof model cannot establish flotation stability of the hall. Missing column-head effects underestimates punching despite modest mean bending, while differential settlement redistributes load to fewer supports.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地下大廳頂板與支承」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Underground hall roofs and supports\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","頂板均載模型不能用來宣稱整個大廳抗浮穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A uniformly loaded roof model cannot establish flotation stability of the hall."],"answer":2,"explanation":"頂板均載模型不能用來宣稱整個大廳抗浮穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A uniformly loaded roof model cannot establish flotation stability of the hall. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b124-v14-21","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地下水位與內部洪水位可分別變動，教材將放空時外壓和充水時淨內壓分開。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Groundwater and internal flood level vary independently; distinguish external pressure when empty from net internal pressure when filled. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=127 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=127 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-21-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"地下水位與內部洪水位可分別變動，教材將放空時外壓和充水時淨內壓分開。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Groundwater and internal flood level vary independently; distinguish external pressure when empty from net internal pressure when filled. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["地下水位與內部洪水位可分別變動，教材將放空時外壓和充水時淨內壓分開。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Groundwater and internal flood level vary independently; distinguish external pressure when empty from net internal pressure when filled.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地下水位與內部洪水位可分別變動，教材將放空時外壓和充水時淨內壓分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Groundwater and internal flood level vary independently; distinguish external pressure when empty from net internal pressure when filled. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b124-v14-22","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=127 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1370.46 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=127 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1370.46 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=127 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1370.46 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=127 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1370.46 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=127 m。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=127 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=127 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=127 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1245.87 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b124-v14-23","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：只看內水位會漏掉空槽時外部地下水控制作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Internal level alone misses groundwater control when the tank is empty. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將兩側水位換成共同高程和表壓後比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert both sides to common elevation and gauge pressure before comparison. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b124-v14-24","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看內水位會漏掉空槽時外部地下水控制作用。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Internal level alone misses groundwater control when the tank is empty. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看內水位會漏掉空槽時外部地下水控制作用。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Internal level alone misses groundwater control when the tank is empty. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只看內水位會漏掉空槽時外部地下水控制作用。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Internal level alone misses groundwater control when the tank is empty.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只看內水位會漏掉空槽時外部地下水控制作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Internal level alone misses groundwater control when the tank is empty. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b124-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「環向受力與接縫柔度」與「水位基準與庫容誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" and \"Level datum and volume uncertainty\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b124-v14-25","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"圓形地下水路的外壓與內壓方向不同，教材均勻環向量級需要按每個水位階段改變淨壓。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"External and internal pressures act oppositely on the circular waterway; update net pressure by water-level stage. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.76 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.76 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-25-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"圓形地下水路的外壓與內壓方向不同，教材均勻環向量級需要按每個水位階段改變淨壓。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"External and internal pressures act oppositely on the circular waterway; update net pressure by water-level stage. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","圓形地下水路的外壓與內壓方向不同，教材均勻環向量級需要按每個水位階段改變淨壓。","多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","External and internal pressures act oppositely on the circular waterway; update net pressure by water-level stage.","Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圓形地下水路的外壓與內壓方向不同，教材均勻環向量級需要按每個水位階段改變淨壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"External and internal pressures act oppositely on the circular waterway; update net pressure by water-level stage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b124-v14-26","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.76 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.59886 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.76 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.59886 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.76 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.59886 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.76 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.59886 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.76 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.76 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.76 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.76 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=7.81714 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b124-v14-27","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略放空後外壓回升會低估外壓主導階段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting external-head recovery after draining understates the external-pressure stage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較環形變形與內外水位，而非僅單側壓力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare ring distortion with both water levels, not one-sided pressure alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b124-v14-28","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略放空後外壓回升會低估外壓主導階段。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting external-head recovery after draining understates the external-pressure stage. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略放空後外壓回升會低估外壓主導階段。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Omitting external-head recovery after draining understates the external-pressure stage. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略放空後外壓回升會低估外壓主導階段。","多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitting external-head recovery after draining understates the external-pressure stage.","Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略放空後外壓回升會低估外壓主導階段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting external-head recovery after draining understates the external-pressure stage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b124-v14-29","title":"水位基準與庫容誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level datum and volume uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「水位零點偏差」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level zero-point bias” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"控制系統把水位轉成剩餘庫容，教材研究共同零點偏移如何讓多感測器一致卻錯估餘量。調蓄控制依賴水位訊號，但壓力式水位計還受氣壓、密度與安裝高程影響。水位誤差乘局部面積可估計一階庫容偏差；若斷面變寬或分艙逐次連通，必須使用完整水位庫容曲線，而非假設全程固定面積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位零點偏差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Controls convert level to reserve volume; examine a shared zero bias that makes sensors agree while misestimating capacity. Storage control depends on level signals, but pressure-based sensors are affected by air pressure, density and installation elevation. Level error times local area estimates first-order volume bias. Widening sections and sequentially connected compartments require the full level-volume relation rather than a constant area across the operating range. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level zero-point bias” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部平面面積=3000 m²；水位零點偏移=0.025 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local plan area=3000 m²; level zero offset=0.025 m. ΔV=AΔh=75 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位零點偏差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level zero-point bias”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-29-k1","title":"水位基準與庫容誤差","titleEn":"Level datum and volume uncertainty","text":"控制系統把水位轉成剩餘庫容，教材研究共同零點偏移如何讓多感測器一致卻錯估餘量。調蓄控制依賴水位訊號，但壓力式水位計還受氣壓、密度與安裝高程影響。","textEn":"Controls convert level to reserve volume; examine a shared zero bias that makes sensors agree while misestimating capacity. Storage control depends on level signals, but pressure-based sensors are affected by air pressure, density and installation elevation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位基準與庫容誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level datum and volume uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","控制系統把水位轉成剩餘庫容，教材研究共同零點偏移如何讓多感測器一致卻錯估餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Controls convert level to reserve volume; examine a shared zero bias that makes sensors agree while misestimating capacity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制系統把水位轉成剩餘庫容，教材研究共同零點偏移如何讓多感測器一致卻錯估餘量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Controls convert level to reserve volume; examine a shared zero bias that makes sensors agree while misestimating capacity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b124-v14-30","title":"水位基準與庫容誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Level datum and volume uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位零點偏差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level zero-point bias” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部平面面積=3000 m²；水位零點偏移=0.025 m。ΔV=AΔh=75 m³。僅把水位零點偏移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.5 m³。邊界：局部等面積一階庫容誤差，變寬及分艙另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local plan area=3000 m²; level zero offset=0.025 m. ΔV=AΔh=75 m³. Increasing only level zero offset by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.5 m³. Boundary: First-order constant-area volume bias; varying width and compartments are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部平面面積=3000 m²；水位零點偏移=0.025 m。ΔV=AΔh=75 m³。僅把水位零點偏移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.5 m³。邊界：局部等面積一階庫容誤差，變寬及分艙另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local plan area=3000 m²; level zero offset=0.025 m. ΔV=AΔh=75 m³. Increasing only level zero offset by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.5 m³. Boundary: First-order constant-area volume bias; varying width and compartments are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位基準與庫容誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level datum and volume uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：局部平面面積=3000 m²；水位零點偏移=0.025 m。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: local plan area=3000 m²; level zero offset=0.025 m. ΔV=AΔh=75 m³.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部平面面積=3000 m²；水位零點偏移=0.025 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local plan area=3000 m²; level zero offset=0.025 m. ΔV=AΔh=75 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b124-v14-31","title":"水位基準與庫容誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level datum and volume uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位零點偏差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level zero-point bias” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。用獨立水準點和人工水尺覆核感測器零點，逐一核對氣壓補償與不同水位的庫容曲線。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge. Check sensor zero against independent benchmarks and a staff gauge, verifying air-pressure compensation and the volume relation at several levels. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「水位零點偏差」的交付需回答：以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。庫容表與水位計使用同一經覆核的高程版本，感測器更換後重驗轉換和警報邏輯，保留原始讀值。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the level zero-point bias handover must address the following evidence: Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge. Use one checked datum revision for volume tables and sensors; after replacement verify conversions and alarm logic while preserving raw readings.","failure":"注意干擾：多支同基準感測器不能互相排除共同高程錯誤。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sensors sharing one reference cannot eliminate a common elevation error by agreement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。用獨立水準點和人工水尺覆核感測器零點，逐一核對氣壓補償與不同水位的庫容曲線。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge. Check sensor zero against independent benchmarks and a staff gauge, verifying air-pressure compensation and the volume relation at several levels. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「水位零點偏差」的交付需回答：以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。庫容表與水位計使用同一經覆核的高程版本，感測器更換後重驗轉換和警報邏輯，保留原始讀值。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the level zero-point bias handover must address the following evidence: Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge. Use one checked datum revision for volume tables and sensors; after replacement verify conversions and alarm logic while preserving raw readings.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位基準與庫容誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level datum and volume uncertainty\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。","頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge.","Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以獨立水準和人工水尺核對零點及庫容表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check zero and volume tables against independent levelling and a staff gauge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b124-v14-32","title":"水位基準與庫容誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level datum and volume uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位零點偏差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level zero-point bias” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"多支同基準感測器不能互相排除共同高程錯誤。多支感測器共用錯誤高程可互相比對一致，卻一致高估剩餘庫容，使控制系統遲判水位上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sensors sharing one reference cannot eliminate a common elevation error by agreement. Several sensors sharing a wrong datum can agree while overestimating remaining volume and delaying recognition of rising water. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：水位誤差乘局部面積可估計一階庫容偏差；若斷面變寬或分艙逐次連通，必須使用完整水位庫容曲線，而非假設全程固定面積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Widening sections and sequentially connected compartments require the full level-volume relation rather than a constant area across the operating range.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「多支水位計讀值相同就能排除共同零點偏差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Matching readings from multiple sensors exclude a shared zero-point bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"多支同基準感測器不能互相排除共同高程錯誤。多支感測器共用錯誤高程可互相比對一致，卻一致高估剩餘庫容，使控制系統遲判水位上升。","textEn":"Sensors sharing one reference cannot eliminate a common elevation error by agreement. Several sensors sharing a wrong datum can agree while overestimating remaining volume and delaying recognition of rising water.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位基準與庫容誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level datum and volume uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","多支同基準感測器不能互相排除共同高程錯誤。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Sensors sharing one reference cannot eliminate a common elevation error by agreement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多支同基準感測器不能互相排除共同高程錯誤。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sensors sharing one reference cannot eliminate a common elevation error by agreement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b124-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b124-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"防洪泵組可用性還取決於供電、出口水頭和共用設備，教材獨立並聯式只作下限模型。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Flood-pump availability also depends on power, discharge head and shared assets; the independent-parallel equation is only a restricted model. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.033 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.033 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"防洪泵組可用性還取決於供電、出口水頭和共用設備，教材獨立並聯式只作下限模型。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Flood-pump availability also depends on power, discharge head and shared assets; the independent-parallel equation is only a restricted model. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["防洪泵組可用性還取決於供電、出口水頭和共用設備，教材獨立並聯式只作下限模型。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Flood-pump availability also depends on power, discharge head and shared assets; the independent-parallel equation is only a restricted model.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"防洪泵組可用性還取決於供電、出口水頭和共用設備，教材獨立並聯式只作下限模型。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Flood-pump availability also depends on power, discharge head and shared assets; the independent-parallel equation is only a restricted model. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b124-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.033 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.001089 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00131769 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.033 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.001089 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00131769 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.033 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.001089 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00131769 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.033 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.001089 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00131769 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["泵站名目排水量大於平均入流就不需要調蓄容積。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.033 無因次。","跌水位能功率可直接當作豎井壁的均勻壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal pumping above mean inflow eliminates the need for storage.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.033 dimensionless.","Drop potential-energy power can be used directly as uniform shaft-wall pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.033 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.033 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b124-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：兩泵正常仍可能因同一高下游水位無法達名目出流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two healthy pumps may fail to achieve rated flow against the same high tailwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"追查每泵供電、閘門和共同出水路徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace each pump feed, gate and shared discharge route. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b124-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩泵正常仍可能因同一高下游水位無法達名目出流。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two healthy pumps may fail to achieve rated flow against the same high tailwater. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩泵正常仍可能因同一高下游水位無法達名目出流。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Two healthy pumps may fail to achieve rated flow against the same high tailwater. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩泵正常仍可能因同一高下游水位無法達名目出流。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Two healthy pumps may fail to achieve rated flow against the same high tailwater.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩泵正常仍可能因同一高下游水位無法達名目出流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two healthy pumps may fail to achieve rated flow against the same high tailwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b124-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響首都圈外郭放水路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洪水事件紀錄需連接雨量、閘門、水位和泵站狀態，教材以事件時間軸檢查資料完整與可追溯性。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Flood records must link rainfall, gates, levels and pump state; use an event timeline to check completeness and traceability. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=123 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=123 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"洪水事件紀錄需連接雨量、閘門、水位和泵站狀態，教材以事件時間軸檢查資料完整與可追溯性。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Flood records must link rainfall, gates, levels and pump state; use an event timeline to check completeness and traceability. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","洪水事件紀錄需連接雨量、閘門、水位和泵站狀態，教材以事件時間軸檢查資料完整與可追溯性。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Flood records must link rainfall, gates, levels and pump state; use an event timeline to check completeness and traceability.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"洪水事件紀錄需連接雨量、閘門、水位和泵站狀態，教材以事件時間軸檢查資料完整與可追溯性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Flood records must link rainfall, gates, levels and pump state; use an event timeline to check completeness and traceability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b124-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=123 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為85.6911 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=123 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 85.6911 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=123 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為85.6911 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=123 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 85.6911 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","頂板平均彎矩不大就不必檢查柱頭沖切及基礎差異。","原創教學假設：設備總數=123 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Small mean roof bending eliminates column punching and differential foundation checks.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=123 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=123 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=123 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.9919 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b124-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：時鐘錯位會把泵啟動先後顛倒，造成錯誤控制評估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Clock offsets reverse apparent pump timing and distort control evaluation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Metropolitan Area Outer Underground Discharge Channel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從一次水位峰回查所有感測器時間與校正版本。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace one level peak through sensor timestamps and calibration revisions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b124-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b124-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時鐘錯位會把泵啟動先後顛倒，造成錯誤控制評估。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Clock offsets reverse apparent pump timing and distort control evaluation. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b124-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時鐘錯位會把泵啟動先後顛倒，造成錯誤控制評估。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Clock offsets reverse apparent pump timing and distort control evaluation. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]},{"id":"b124-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","時鐘錯位會把泵啟動先後顛倒，造成錯誤控制評估。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Clock offsets reverse apparent pump timing and distort control evaluation.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時鐘錯位會把泵啟動先後顛倒，造成錯誤控制評估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clock offsets reverse apparent pump timing and distort control evaluation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b124","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b124-history"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
